## 2. KHAZNA v3 — LAPIS LUX (NON-NEGOTIABLES)

### 2.1 Visual Identity

Daftar is a **premium monochrome financial tool** with **one luminous accent** (lapis as light). Every screen communicates:
- **Trust** — tabular numerals, strict grid, semantic red/green only for money states.
- **Waqār (restraint)** — ~95% Onyx/Bone greyscale; no gold, no teal, no rainbow.
- **Salāsa (depth through light)** — Khazna Float cards, lapis halos on the single CTA per screen.

**Reject on sight (CRITICAL DEFECT):**
- **Lapis as fill** on any button, card, FAB, or chip — see §2.4
- `FilledButton`, `ElevatedButton`, or `MaterialButton` with lapis/primary **background fill**
- Material `Card()` — use **`DaftarCard`**
- Material `TextField` for product forms — use **`DaftarTextField`**
- `ListTile` — custom-composed rows only
- `AlertDialog` — bottom sheets only
- Default `SnackBar` / naked `CircularProgressIndicator` as primary loading
- Hard-coded `Color(0xFF...)` outside `AppColors`
- Deprecated tokens: `darkPrimary`, `darkAccent`, `darkSurface`, `lightPrimary`, etc. — use v3 canonical names only

### 2.2 Dark Mode as Canvas (Default)

Dark mode is the PRIMARY canvas (true OLED):
- Scaffold: `AppColors.surface0` (`#000000`)
- Cards: `AppColors.surface2` (`#121214`) with **Khazna Float** — `AppGlows.khazaFloat` + `0.5px borderSubtle` + top `innerTopHighlight` — **NEVER Material drop-shadow on dark**
- Text: `inkPrimary` (`#F5F5F5`) — never pure white on pure black
- Depth: stepped surfaces `surface1` → `surface6` (+6 luminance per step)
- Light mode: `surface0Light` (Bone `#F8F7F4`), cards `surface1Light`, shadows `AppGlows.shadowFloat`

### 2.3 Color Discipline — Three Citizens Only

- ZERO ad-hoc colors. Every reference resolves to `AppColors` / `AppGlows` / `AppTextStyles`.
- **Monochrome:** `surface*`, `ink*`, `borderSubtle`, `borderStrong` for all chrome and text.
- **Semantic (money only):** `debt`, `payment`, `warning`, `error`, `success` — never generic "red/green" literals.
- **Lapis:** borders + `AppGlows` halos ONLY — see §2.4.
- NEVER `Color.withOpacity()` with arbitrary decimals — use named alpha tokens from design system.
- **ONE lapis-glow moment per visible screen** (FAB OR primary CTA OR focused input OR hero brand mark — never two).

### 2.4 ⛔ THE LAPIS FIREWALL — READ BEFORE EVERY UI CHANGE

> **Lapis is light, not paint.** Violating this is a **CRITICAL DEFECT**.

| ✅ PERMITTED | ❌ FORBIDDEN |
|---|---|
| `boxShadow: AppGlows.ctaRest` (`glowMd`) on Primary CTA | `backgroundColor: AppColors.lapis400` on buttons |
| `BorderSide(color: AppColors.lapis400, width: 0.5)` on Primary CTA | `FilledButton` / `ElevatedButton` with lapis fill |
| `AppGlows.khazaFloat` on dark floating cards | Lapis gradient on card/content surfaces |
| `1.5px lapis400` focus ring on `DaftarTextField` | `color: AppColors.lapis400` on `Text` or `Icon` (except info banners) |
| `2dp` lapis tab indicator / bottom-nav stripe | `Theme.of(context).colorScheme.primary` as button fill without overriding |
| Info banner bg: `lapis800` / `lapis50` (sole fill exception) | More than ONE lapis glow target per screen |

**`DaftarButton` Primary anatomy (MANDATORY):**
- **Fill:** `AppColors.surface2` (dark) or `AppColors.surface1Light` (light) — **monochrome**
- **Border:** `0.5px` `AppColors.lapis400`
- **Halo:** `AppGlows.ctaRest` (`glowMd`)
- **Text:** `AppColors.inkPrimary` / `inkPrimaryLight` — NOT white-on-blue unless destructive variant
- **Press:** scale `0.97`, halo → `AppGlows.ctaPressed`, `HapticService.buttonPress()`

If your button looks like a **blue rectangle**, you built it wrong.

